cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CareFed-TrustLab: Privacy-Preserving and Trustworthy Federated Learning for Connected-Health Research"
message: "If you use this research prototype, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Khyzer"
    given-names: "Hira"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hirakhyzer/CareFed-TrustLab"
abstract: "An independent academic research prototype for auditable privacy-preserving federated learning in connected healthcare using synthetic multi-site health telemetry, privacy-aware update handling, robust aggregation, malicious-client experiments, calibration, subgroup auditing, explainability, MATLAB analysis, and a hash-chained experiment ledger."
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - trustworthy AI
  - healthcare AI
  - privacy-preserving machine learning
  - secure aggregation
  - fairness audit
  - calibration
  - explainability
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
